---
import BlogLayout from "../../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title =
  "Product Copy and Landing Page Copywriting Services | Matteo Arellano";

const description =
  "Results-driven product copy and landing page services for businesses that need clearer product explanations, stronger search visibility, AI visibility, multi-region content, and better conversion paths.";

const canonical =
  "https://matteoarellano.com/services/product-copy-landing-pages/";

const serviceJsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  name: "Product copy and landing page copywriting services",
  serviceType:
    "Product copywriting, landing page copywriting, SEO landing pages, multi-region product pages, AI visibility copy",
  provider: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Matteo Arellano",
    url: "https://matteoarellano.com/",
  },
  areaServed: "Worldwide",
  url: canonical,
  description,
});

const faqJsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "Who should hire you for product copy and landing pages?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Companies should hire me when their product needs clearer explanations, stronger search visibility, better conversion paths, or market-specific landing pages across languages, currencies, regions, or user journeys.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What results have you helped create?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "I have helped improve organic visibility by more than 200%, supported conversion improvements above 50%, worked on pages with thousands of daily users, and built pages for products that needed stronger search alignment and clearer customer language.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "How do you write landing page copy?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "I combine product research, customer questions, search intent, Google results, AI visibility checks, analytics, event data, page structure, and technical SEO signals to write pages that explain the product clearly and help users move forward.",
      },
    },
  ],
});
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={serviceJsonLd} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJsonLd} />

  <main class="article-page">
    <article class="article-shell">
      <a class="blog-back-link" href="/#services">← Back to services</a>

      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="article-kicker">Product copy and landing pages</span>

        <h1>
          Landing page copy for products that need to rank, explain, and convert
        </h1>

        <p class="article-intro">
          If your product needs clearer explanations, stronger search
          visibility, better AI visibility, or landing pages that turn traffic
          into real action, I can help you write the page from product research,
          customer intent, analytics, and real user questions.
        </p>

        <div class="article-meta">
          <span>100+ landing pages created</span>
          <span>+200% Google Search Console impression growth</span>
          <span>+50% conversion growth</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="article-content">
        <div class="personal-note">
          <p>
            I’m
            <a
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/matteoarellano/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              Matteo Arellano
            </a>. I write product copy and landing pages by combining technical
            SEO, analytics, AI visibility, product research, and customer
            language. The goal is simple: make your product easier to find,
            easier to understand, and easier to choose.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>If your product requires more than a basic landing page</h2>

        <p>
          Some pages need a clean explanation of one offer. Others need a page
          that handles complexity without making the user work too hard.
        </p>

        <p>I can help when your product requires:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Clearer product positioning for high-intent searches.</li>
          <li>
            Landing pages for different markets, regions, currencies, or
            languages.
          </li>
          <li>Better explanations for complex product specifications.</li>
          <li>
            Pages that support premium pricing with stronger proof and clarity.
          </li>
          <li>Copy that answers customer doubts before the next step.</li>
          <li>
            Alternative naming when customers search differently from your
            internal product name.
          </li>
          <li>Better page structure for SEO, AI visibility, and conversion.</li>
          <li>
            Copy connected to GA4, GTM, Amplitude, heatmaps, feedback forms, or
            user behavior.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          If your current page gets traffic but users still hesitate, the issue
          may be the way the offer is explained, the questions left unanswered,
          or the gap between how your team describes the product and how
          customers search for it.
        </p>

        <h2>Results I have helped create</h2>

        <div class="impact-grid">
          <div class="impact-card">
            <h3>200%+ more impressions</h3>
            <p>
              I helped improve organic visibility by more than 200% by making
              product pages clearer, better aligned with search intent, and more
              specific to what customers were actually trying to find.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="impact-card">
            <h3>Top 2 non-branded rankings</h3>
            <p>
              I have worked on pages that reached top positions for important
              non-branded searches by improving product naming, page structure,
              customer language, and commercial relevance.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="impact-card">
            <h3>50%+ conversion improvement</h3>
            <p>
              I helped improve conversion performance by more than 50% over a
              short period by working on page clarity, user intent, content
              structure, tracking, and feedback from real behavior.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="impact-card">
            <h3>Thousands of daily users</h3>
            <p>
              I have worked on campaigns and pages that grew from early traffic
              to thousands of daily users by improving search visibility,
              landing page relevance, and high-intent query coverage.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Problems I usually help fix</h2>

        <div class="comparison-table is-readable">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>If your page has this problem</th>
                <th>What it usually means</th>
                <th>How I would improve it</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>The page gets impressions but weak clicks.</td>
                <td>
                  The title, heading, offer, or snippet may be missing the
                  language people use when they search.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Improve search intent alignment, page title, headings, product
                  naming, and the first explanation.
                </td>
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>The page gets traffic but users stop before converting.</td>
                <td>
                  The product may still feel unclear, risky, expensive,
                  unavailable, or hard to compare.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Add stronger proof, clearer next steps, objection handling,
                  pricing clarity, availability details, and funnel-specific
                  copy.
                </td>
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td
                  >Your product works across countries, currencies, or
                  languages.</td
                >
                <td>
                  The same product may need different explanations depending on
                  the market, payment method, region, trust level, or user
                  expectation.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Build market-specific sections, local search wording,
                  multilingual structure, hreflang awareness, and clearer
                  regional positioning.
                </td>
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td
                  >Your team uses one product name, but customers search
                  another.</td
                >
                <td>
                  Internal naming and customer language are creating a
                  visibility gap.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Add alternative identifiers, category language, practical
                  descriptions, and headings that match how people search.
                </td>
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Your product is premium, but the page feels generic.</td>
                <td>
                  The page may be asking users to pay more without explaining
                  the value clearly enough.
                </td>
                <td>
                  Strengthen the product explanation, proof points, trust
                  signals, comparison logic, and value story.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>What I do before writing the page</h2>

        <p>
          I start by understanding the product in depth. I want to know what it
          does, who it helps, what users need before making a decision, what
          makes the offer valuable, and where the current page creates friction.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also use research tools I have built to speed up the investigation.
          They help me inspect page structure, search results, customer
          questions, metadata, internal links, technical SEO signals,
          multilingual signals, and gaps in the current page.
        </p>

        <div class="audit-checklist">
          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Product research</h3>
            <p>
              I review the offer, product specifications, market differences,
              value proposition, user doubts, and the real customer journey.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Search and AI visibility research</h3>
            <p>
              I compare what people search with what Google and AI systems
              surface. I look for missing questions, weak answers, fragmented
              explanations, and opportunities to become more visible.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Customer language</h3>
            <p>
              I compare the language used by your team with the language used by
              customers. This is especially useful when product names,
              categories, or market terms differ across regions.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Analytics and behavior</h3>
            <p>
              When data is available, I use GA4, GTM, Amplitude, event data,
              feedback forms, and heatmap-style tools to understand where users
              hesitate or drop off.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Page structure</h3>
            <p>
              I organize the page so the most important explanation appears
              early, the objections are answered in the right order, and the CTA
              feels connected to the product promise.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Technical SEO checks</h3>
            <p>
              I check titles, headings, internal links, metadata, canonicals,
              hreflang needs, structured data, and page quality signals that
              affect visibility.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>
          If your audience is multi-language, multi-currency, or multi-region
        </h2>

        <p>
          This is where landing page copy becomes more valuable. A product can
          be technically the same across markets, while the questions users ask
          are completely different.
        </p>

        <p>I can help if your business has:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Different currencies, payment methods, or pricing expectations.
          </li>
          <li>
            Different languages where direct translation weakens the page.
          </li>
          <li>
            Different regional trust signals, regulations, availability, or
            support details.
          </li>
          <li>Different names for the same product across markets.</li>
          <li>
            Different conversion flows depending on country, location, or
            customer type.
          </li>
          <li>
            Different search demand depending on how people describe the same
            need.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          In those cases, I work on the page so users feel that the product was
          explained for their market, not copied from a generic template.
        </p>

        <h2>How the final page becomes stronger</h2>

        <div class="comparison-table is-readable">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Before</th>
                <th>After</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>

            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Generic headline and broad product description.</td>
                <td>Clear value proposition connected to customer intent.</td>
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Internal product names customers may not recognize.</td>
                <td
                  >Customer language, alternative identifiers, and
                  search-friendly wording.</td
                >
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Weak explanation of how the product works.</td>
                <td
                  >Specific sections that answer doubts before users click or
                  leave.</td
                >
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Same copy used across markets.</td>
                <td
                  >Market-aware copy for different languages, regions,
                  currencies, and journeys.</td
                >
              </tr>

              <tr>
                <td>Landing page written separately from analytics.</td>
                <td
                  >Copy shaped by real behavior, funnel signals, search data,
                  and customer questions.</td
                >
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>What you get</h2>

        <div class="audit-checklist">
          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Landing page copy</h3>
            <p>
              A clearer page structure with headings, sections, product
              explanations, proof points, objections, FAQs, and CTA copy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Search intent mapping</h3>
            <p>
              A breakdown of the customer questions, search terms, and content
              gaps the page should answer.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>SEO and AI visibility recommendations</h3>
            <p>
              Practical improvements for titles, headings, internal links,
              structured information, entity clarity, and answer coverage.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-check">
            <h3>Conversion-focused page feedback</h3>
            <p>
              Notes on what may be blocking users from moving forward and which
              parts of the page need stronger clarity or proof.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>When to work with me</h2>

        <p>
          Work with me if your product needs to be easier to understand, easier
          to find, and easier to trust.
        </p>

        <p>
          This is especially useful when your page needs to support SEO growth,
          AI visibility, product positioning, paid traffic, multi-region
          expansion, or conversion improvement.
        </p>

        <div class="article-cta">
          <h2>Need a landing page that explains the product better?</h2>

          <p>
            Send me the product, the current page, and the questions your users
            keep asking. I will review where the page is unclear, where the
            search opportunity is, and how the copy can become more useful for
            both users and search.
          </p>

          <a class="article-cta-button" href="/free-visibility-check/#calendar">
            Request a visibility check
          </a>

          <p class="cta-note">
            Best fit: products with search demand, product complexity,
            multilingual or multi-region audiences, or pages where traffic is
            already coming in but the page needs to convert better.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BlogLayout>
